BT 1 0 0 1 0 123 Tm /F1 9 Tf 12 TL (The large-scale structure of the universe contains features that Lambda-CDM cosmology cannot explain: voids too large,) Tj T* (quasar groups too extended, bulk flows too fast, spin alignments too correlated, and dipoles that disagree. Ten anomalies) Tj T* (spanning scales from individual galaxies to the 1.7 Gpc Giant GRB Ring are resolved through the vacuum coherence) Tj T* (function C = C0 x exp\(-alpha x gamma_eff\). Each anomaly is identified as a coherence fossil -- a relic of the primordial) Tj T* (high-coherence state preserved in the geometry, kinematics, or composition of cosmic structure. The KBC Void is a) Tj T* (self-stabilizing low-gamma_eff region. Large Quasar Groups are fossils of primordial coherence domains exceeding 370) Tj T* (Mpc. The Giant GRB Ring traces a spherical decoherence front. Anomalous bulk flows record coherent velocity memory.) Tj T* (Galaxy spin alignments preserve primordial angular momentum correlations. The cosmic dipole tension, missing galactic) Tj T* (baryons, Lyman-alpha blobs, primordial magnetic fields, and the cosmic coincidence problem each yield to the same) Tj T* (principle: the universe remembers its coherent past, and these memories are written into its largest structures. This paper) Tj T* (extends Papers 120 \(Structure Formation\), 84 \(Z2 Symmetry\), and 5 \(REQMT\) in the AIIT-THRESI series.) Tj T* ET
